#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:8
msgid "shared-memory interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `shared-memory` interface allows two snaps to communicate with each "
"other using a specific predefined shared-memory path or directory in `/dev/"
"shm`, an area of a POSIX-compliant filesystem reserved for shared memory. "
"The location is defined by one snap and connected to from another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:12
msgid "Requires snapd version *2.54+* ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:15
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid "**no** by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"**yes** when `private` is enabled, or with snaps from the same publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-privileged-"
"interfaces>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid "**no** for plugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:0
msgid "**yes** for slots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:23
msgid ""
"The `shared-memory` slot is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-unsupported>`. The `shared-memory` plug is "
"supported for parallel instances only if it sets `private: true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:26
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"`shared-memory` (slot and plug): optional, arbitrary identifier for the "
"shared memory area(s) defined in the slot. A consumer snap must use the same "
"identifier as the provider snap in order to work on the same shared memory "
"object(s). Defaults to either local slot name or local plug name for slot/"
"plug definitions respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"`private` (plug): when `true`, creates a directory that is only accessible "
"to the snap. This directory has read/write permissions, is mounted over `/"
"dev/shm`, and permits an auto-connection to the `system:shared-memory` slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"`read` (slot): list of *read-only* paths (after the implicit `/dev/shm/`) to "
"be exposed to a consuming snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"`write` (slot): list of *read and write* paths (after the implicit `/dev/shm/"
"`) to be exposed to a consuming snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"The `read` and `write` attributes are used on the slot side to specify the "
"names of the shared memory objects being shared (in read-only mode for "
"`read`, and with full read-write mode for `write`); the prefix `/dev/shm/` "
"is implicit and must not be specified. Both attributes can be specified "
"simultaneously for different paths, but the two values should not duplicate "
"each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:36
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:38
msgid "An example plug definition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
" my-ipc:\n"
"  interface: shared-memory\n"
"  # this could be omitted since we already adjusted ​the plug name\n"
"  # to match the slot's shared-memory name:\n"
"  shared-memory: my-ipc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:49
msgid ""
"A matching slot definition which would auto-connect if in a snap from the "
"same publisher:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:51
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
" shmem:\n"
"  interface: shared-memory\n"
"  shared-memory: my-ipc\n"
"  write: [ students ]  # gives read/write access to /dev/shm/students\n"
"  read: [ teachers ]   # gives readonly access to /dev/shm/teachers\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:60
msgid "Creating `private` shared memory for the snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:62
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  shared-memory:\n"
"    private: true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:68
msgid ""
"When `private: true` is used,  the shared-memory interface is automatically "
"connected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/shared-memory-interface.md:70
msgid ""
"$ snap connections <example-private-shared-memory-snap>\n"
"Interface      Plug                      Slot            Notes\n"
"shared-memory  os-release:shared-memory  :shared-memory  -\n"
msgstr ""

